.TH TEATHER 1 "August 2026" "Teather 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
teather \- control the Teather Linux USB desktop client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B teather
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B teather
uses the per-user Teather D-Bus service to inspect phones, connect or disconnect
the temporary TCP tunnel, manage remembered phones, and run diagnostics.
Raw ADB serial numbers are not displayed or stored.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status [--json]
Show connection state, counters, and coarse errors.
.TP
.B devices [--json]
List detected and remembered phones using locally salted identifiers.
.TP
.B connect [DEVICE_ID]
Connect an approved phone. An interactive choice is required when several are eligible.
.TP
.B disconnect
Stop the tunnel and clean resources proven to be owned by Teather.
.TP
.B device approve DEVICE_ID [--yes]
Approve a locally connected phone. Without
.BR --yes ,
confirmation is requested on the terminal.
.TP
.B device rename DEVICE_ID NAME
Set the local display name for a remembered phone.
.TP
.B device forget DEVICE_ID
Remove a remembered phone and its preferences.
.TP
.B autoconnect on|off DEVICE_ID
Set safe auto-connect for an approved phone. Auto-connect never starts a stopped Android relay.
.TP
.B failover on|off
Arm or hold dormant automatic failover. When on (the default), Teather installs a
worse-metric backup default route and an additive DNS entry so traffic moves to
the phone automatically once Wi-Fi or Ethernet is lost. When off, Teather still
connects but stays dormant until this is set back on.
.TP
.B upstream auto|cellular|wifi|ethernet
Choose which of the phone's transports the relay binds outbound sockets to
(default cellular). Changing this while connected restarts only the phone's relay
binding; the teather0 interface, tunnel, routes, and DNS are untouched.
.TP
.B diagnose [--json]
Run read-only diagnostics.
.TP
.B recover [--json]
Clean only journaled resources, then report diagnostics.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Teather carries IPv4 TCP, virtual DNS over UDP and TCP, and general UDP (the
latter over tun2proxy's udpgw stream, terminated by the phone). IPv6 is
unsupported. Teather does not change Wi-Fi, Ethernet, persistent
NetworkManager profiles, firewall rules, or physical-interface state. It creates
one in-memory, non-persistent NetworkManager connection for teather0 whose DNS is
additive: the physical link's resolver stays first while it is present.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/teather/config.json
Mode-0600 preferences, the auto-failover setting, and locally salted device
identifiers.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/teather/RECOVERY.md.gz
Offline recovery instructions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR teatherd (1),
.BR teather-gtk (1)
